#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:72
msgid "Now, let's begin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:74
msgid "Go to |link_appinventor_login|, and click \"online tool\" to login. You will require a Google account to register with MIT App Inventor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:80
msgid "After logging in, navigate to **Projects** -> **Import project (.aia) from my computer**. Subsequently, upload the ``Bluetooth_controlled_lock.aia`` file located in the path ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_esp01\\bluetooth\\05-Bluetooth_environmental_monitor``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:82
msgid "You can also directly download here: :download:`Bluetooth_Environmental_Monitor.aia</_static/other/Bluetooth_Environmental_Monitor.aia>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:87
msgid "Upon uploading the ``.aia`` file, you will see the application on the MIT App Inventor software. This is a pre-configured template. You can modify this template after you have familiarized yourself with MIT App Inventor through the following steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:89
msgid "In MIT App Inventor, you have 2 primary sections: the **Designer** and the **Blocks**. You can switch between these two sections in the upper right corner of the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:93
msgid "The **Designer** allows you to add buttons, text, screens, and modify the overall aesthetic of your application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:97
msgid "Next, there's the **Blocks** section. This section lets you craft custom functionalities for your app, allowing you to program each component on the app's GUI to achieve desired features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:101
msgid "To install the application on a smartphone, navigate to the **Build** tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:105
msgid "You can generate a ``.apk`` file. After selecting this option, a page will appear allowing you to choose between downloading a ``.apk`` file or scanning a QR code for installation. Follow the installation guide to complete the application installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:107
msgid "You also download our pre-compiled APK here: :download:`Bluetooth_Environmental_Monitor.apk</_static/other/Bluetooth_Environmental_Monitor.apk>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:109
msgid "If you wish to upload this app to Google Play or another app marketplace, you can generate a ``.aab`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:113
msgid "3. Upload the Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:115
msgid "Open the ``05-Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_esp01\\bluetooth\\05-Bluetooth_environmental_monitor``, or copy this code into **Arduino IDE**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:118
msgid "To install the library, use the Arduino Library Manager and search for **\"DHT sensor library\"** and install it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:124
msgid "After selecting the correct board and port, click the **Upload** button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:126
msgid "Open the Serial monitor(set baudrate to **9600**) to view debug messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:129
msgid "4. App and Bluetooth module Connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:131
msgid "Ensure that the application created earlier is installed on your smartphone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:133
msgid "Initially, turn on **Bluetooth** on your smartphone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:139
msgid "Navigate to the **Bluetooth settings** on your smartphone and look for names like **JDY-31-SPP**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:145
msgid "After clicking it, agree to the **Pair** request in the pop-up window. If prompted for a pairing code, please enter \"1234\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:151
msgid "Now open the newly installed **Environmental Monitor** APP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:157
msgid "In the APP, click on **Connect** button to establish a connection between the APP and Bluetooth module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:163
msgid "This page displays a list of all paired Bluetooth devices. Choose the ``xx.xx.xx.xx.xx.xx JDY-31-SPP`` option from the list. The name of each device is listed next to its MAC address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:169
msgid "If you don't see any devices on the page shown above, it could be because this app is not authorized to scan for nearby devices. In such a case, you will need to adjust the settings manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:171
msgid "To access the **APP Info** page, long-press the app icon and select it. Alternatively, if you have another method to reach this page, use that instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:177
msgid "Navigate to the **Permissions** page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:183
msgid "To enable the APP to scan for nearby devices, go to **Nearby devices** and select **Always**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:189
msgid "Now, restart the APP and repeat steps 5 and 6 to successfully connect to Bluetooth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/10-iot_Bluetooth_environmental_monitor.rst:191
msgid "After a successful connection, you will be redirected to the main page where it will display temperature and humidity."
msgstr ""

